# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: nasha-update-tail-in-bounds
why: Nasha*_Update copies the last partial block with memcpy(..., len/8+1), one byte more than the input holds
why: when the remaining bit length is a multiple of 8, which is every byte-oriented call (AddressSanitizer
why: global-buffer-overflow past the input, CI run 45581879065). Final masks every bit at or after the bit count
why: (or clears the word when it is a multiple of 64), so that byte never reached the digest. (len+7)/8 copies the
why: bytes that hold input bits only; every digest is unchanged.
file: upstream/opt/Nasha.c
count: 2
find: memcpy((unsigned char *)state->M, sp, len/8+1);
replace: memcpy((unsigned char *)state->M, sp, (len+7)/8);
